|name2 = Mystic Egg: N005
|name3 = Hitman Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystic Egg: N005''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Hitman Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
This unit is a dangerous specialist attacker geared to counter Traitless enemies, very similar to [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], with great attack power, average survivability and medium effective range, though his blindspot is somewhat large. Compared to the likes of [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] and [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]], he isn't good as a generalist due to having less effective range and just about the same DPS, limiting his selection of potential targets. What sets Hitman Cat aside is his combination of abilities and stats. Traitless enemies are notoriously difficult to find counters against, and many of them either don't deal enough damage to falter such threats, or can't even reach them in the first place, similar to [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]]. Hitman Cat finds particular use in countering a wide array of enemy midrangers, [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]], pushers, and more, provided his blindspot is covered. His Freeze Immunity and speed also makes him suitable for fighting [[Henry]], as he cannot be disabled and will easily make it into Henry's blindspot. Though he is indeed a bit overpriced, he does have his own uses and is a formidable option against plenty of Traitless foes, reaching up to 12K effective DPS at Lv.50, making it well worth the investment.

