==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]], Ancient Egg: N005's and [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N001]]'s names did not have colons.
*Ancient Egg: N005, [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N004]] and [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N003]] are currently the only [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]] whose [[True Form]]s do not have [[Behemoth Slayer]].
*Hitman Cat's weapon is a [[wikipedia:FGM-148 Javelin|FGM-148 Javelin]].
*Hitman Cat can be seen as a foil to [[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]]. Both are sunglasses-wearing ranged [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Egg]] units that have damage-increasing [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] abilities and are implied to be incompetent at their jobs, with Hitman Cat being questioned by police more times than he has killed his targets and Cop Cat chewing hot-dog-flavored gum to stay awake as he patrols a city with a crime rate of 120%. They contrast in how their professions oppose each other and Hitman Cat is a more offensive unit that deals higher damage less frequently in a wider area, with exactly half the health of Cop Cat, Massive Damage instead of Strong Against, and a much longer attack cycle. Hitman Cat's blind spot is also equal to Cop Cat's range.

